    ("Number Needed to Harm (NNH) Inverse of Absolute Risk Increase (1 / ARI)", "Biostatistics", "General Principles", "number of patients exposed to therapeutic agent required for one additional patient to experience a harmful adverse effect; calculated as reciprocal of absolute risk increase", "USMLE Biostatistics Specifications", "https://www.usmle.org/"),
    ("Type I Error (Alpha) False Positive Rate Rejection of True Null Hypothesis", "Biostatistics", "General Principles", "concluding there is a statistically significant treatment effect when in reality no true difference exists; conventionally set at significance threshold p < 0.05", "USMLE Biostatistics Core Curriculum", "https://www.usmle.org/"),
    ("Type II Error (Beta) False Negative Rate Failure to Reject False Null Hypothesis", "Biostatistics", "General Principles", "concluding there is no difference between study arms when a true difference actually exists; directly linked to statistical power (Power = 1 - Beta)", "USMLE Biostatistics Core Curriculum", "https://www.usmle.org/"),
    ("Statistical Power (1 - Beta) Probability of Correctly Rejecting False Null Hypothesis", "Biostatistics", "General Principles", "likelihood of detecting a true therapeutic difference when one exists; increased by enlarging sample size, increasing effect size, reducing variance, or raising alpha threshold", "USMLE Biostatistics Curriculum", "https://www.usmle.org/"),
    ("Confounding Variable Distortion of Exposure-Outcome Relationship by Extraneous Factor", "Biostatistics", "General Principles", "extraneous variable associated with both exposure and outcome that is not an intermediate on the causal pathway; controlled by randomization, restriction, matching, or stratification", "USMLE Epidemiology Specifications", "https://www.usmle.org/"),
    ("Effect Modification Biological Interaction Distinct Association Across Strata", "Biostatistics", "General Principles", "external variable that modulates the magnitude of association between exposure and outcome such that stratified analysis demonstrates significantly different stratum-specific effect estimates", "USMLE Epidemiology Specifications", "https://www.usmle.org/"),
    ("Selection Bias Non-Random Allocation Berkson Bias Healthy Worker Effect", "Biostatistics", "General Principles", "systematic error in subject recruitment or retention causing study population to unrepresent true target population; includes hospital admission bias and volunteer attrition bias", "USMLE Epidemiology Curriculum", "https://www.usmle.org/"),
    ("Recall Bias Differential Accuracy of Historical Exposure in Case-Control Studies", "Biostatistics", "General Principles", "subjects with adverse outcome recall past exposures with greater or lesser accuracy than healthy controls, distorting measured odds ratio; minimized by blinding or verifying records", "USMLE Epidemiology Curriculum", "https://www.usmle.org/"),
    ("Lead-Time Bias Apparent Survival Prolongation Due to Early Detection by Screening", "Biostatistics", "General Principles", "screening detects disease earlier in its natural history without altering the ultimate date of death, creating artificial statistical illusion of prolonged post-diagnosis survival", "USMLE Biostatistics Specifications", "https://www.usmle.org/"),
    ("Length-Time Bias Disproportionate Detection of Slowly Progressive Indolent Disease by Screening", "Biostatistics", "General Principles", "routine periodic screening tests preferentially detect asymptomatic, slowly growing, indolent lesions with longer preclinical phases, overestimating screening clinical efficacy", "USMLE Biostatistics Specifications", "https://www.usmle.org/"),
    ("Medical Ethics Autonomy Patient Right to Self-Determination and Informed Refusal", "Ethics", "General Principles", "competent patients have the ethical and legal right to accept or refuse any medical intervention based on personal values, even if refusal results in disability or death", "AMA Code of Medical Ethics", "https://code-medical-ethics.ama-assn.org/"),
    ("Medical Ethics Beneficence Acting in Patient Best Interest Moral Obligation to Promote Health", "Ethics", "General Principles", "physicians have positive fiduciary duty to act for patient benefit, weigh potential therapeutic advantages against clinical burdens, and actively optimize well-being", "AMA Code of Medical Ethics", "https://code-medical-ethics.ama-assn.org/"),
    ("Medical Ethics Nonmaleficence Primum Non Nocere Minimization of Foreseeable Harm", "Ethics", "General Principles", "fundamental imperative to avoid inflicting unnecessary harm; requires balancing treatment side effects and potential procedural complications against anticipated clinical benefits", "AMA Code of Medical Ethics", "https://code-medical-ethics.ama-assn.org/"),
    ("Medical Ethics Justice Fair Allocation of Scarce Medical Resources and Equal Treatment", "Ethics", "General Principles", "principle of distributive fairness mandating equitable healthcare distribution without discrimination based on socioeconomic status, race, gender, age, or personal background", "AMA Code of Medical Ethics", "https://code-medical-ethics.ama-assn.org/"),
    ("Informed Consent Required Elements Decision-Making Capacity Disclosure Comprehension Voluntariness", "Ethics", "General Principles", "valid consent requires patient capacity, physician disclosure of diagnosis, risks, benefits, and alternatives, demonstrated patient understanding, and voluntary authorization without coercion", "AMA Code of Medical Ethics: Informed Consent", "https://code-medical-ethics.ama-assn.org/"),
    ("Surrogate Decision-Making Substituted Judgment Standard vs Best Interest Principle", "Ethics", "General Principles", "surrogate decision-maker must first apply substituted judgment deciding what incapacitated patient would have chosen based on known prior values, falling back to best interests only if values unknown", "AMA Code of Medical Ethics", "https://code-medical-ethics.ama-assn.org/"),
    ("Surrogate Hierarchy Legal Priority Healthcare Proxy Spouse Adult Children Parents Siblings", "Ethics", "General Principles", "in the absence of designated durable power of attorney for healthcare, legal priority for surrogate decision-making typically follows spouse, adult children, parents, and adult siblings", "AMA Code of Medical Ethics", "https://code-medical-ethics.ama-assn.org/"),
    ("Minor Patient Confidentiality Exceptions Reproductive Health Contraception STI Treatment Substance Abuse", "Ethics", "General Principles", "unemancipated minors can provide independent confidential consent for diagnosis and treatment of sexually transmitted infections, contraception, pregnancy care, and substance use rehabilitation", "AAP Policy Statement on Confidentiality in Adolescent Care", "https://www.aap.org/"),
    ("Medical Error Disclosure Ethical Duty of Prompt Full Transparency and Institutional Apology", "Ethics", "General Principles", "physicians must promptly disclose medical errors resulting in harm directly to patient or family, explain root causes, outline remedial actions taken, and answer questions truthfully", "AMA Code of Medical Ethics: Patient Safety", "https://code-medical-ethics.ama-assn.org/"),
    ("Physician-Assisted Suicide Legal and Ethical Boundaries Respecting Palliative Care and Voluntary Refusal", "Ethics", "General Principles", "ethical obligation to provide aggressive palliative symptom management and honor patient rights to refuse or withdraw life support, distinguished from active euthanasia", "AMA Code of Medical Ethics: End of Life Care", "https://code-medical-ethics.ama-assn.org/"),

    # 101-130: Reproductive Physiology, Embryology & Teratology
    ("SRY Gene Sex-Determining Region on Y Chromosome Testis-Determining Factor (TDF) Sertoli/Leydig Differentiation", "Genetics", "Pregnancy", "SRY gene on short arm of Y chromosome encodes TDF directing indifferent gonadal ridge to develop into testes; Sertoli cells secrete anti-Mullerian hormone and Leydig cells secrete testosterone", "ACOG Clinical Practice Guidelines on Sexual Differentiation", "https://www.acog.org/"),
    ("Mullerian (Paramesonephric) Duct Derivations Fallopian Tubes Uterus and Upper One-Third of Vagina", "Anatomy", "Pregnancy", "in the absence of anti-Mullerian hormone (AMH / MIF), paramesonephric ducts automatically develop into female internal genitalia, while lower two-thirds of vagina arises from urogenital sinus", "ACOG Committee Opinion on Mullerian Anomalies", "https://www.acog.org/"),
    ("Wolffian (Mesonephric) Duct Derivations Epididymis Vas Deferens Seminal Vesicles and Ejaculatory Duct", "Anatomy", "Pregnancy", "testosterone from fetal Leydig cells stimulates stabilization and elongation of mesonephric ducts into male internal genital duct system (mnemonic: SEED)", "AUA Practice Guidelines on Male Genital Embryology", "https://www.auanet.org/"),
    ("Dihydrotestosterone (DHT) 5alpha-Reductase External Male Genitalia Differentiation Prostate and Scrotum", "Physiology", "Endocrine", "intracellular conversion of testosterone to potent DHT by 5alpha-reductase in target tissues drives development of penis, scrotum, and prostate from genital tubercle, swellings, and folds", "Endocrine Society Guidelines on Male Hypogonadism", "https://www.endocrine.org/"),
    ("Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome (AIS) Complete 46,XY Nonfunctional Androgen Receptor Female External Phenotype", "Genetics", "Endocrine", "mutations in X-linked androgen receptor gene; normal male testosterone and AMH levels, rudimentary/absent uterus and upper vagina, cryptorchid testes, and female breast development", "Endocrine Society Guidelines on DSD", "https://www.endocrine.org/"),
    ("5alpha-Reductase Deficiency 46,XY Impaired Testosterone Conversion Virilization at Puberty", "Genetics", "Endocrine", "autosomal recessive defect in 5alpha-reductase type 2 preventing DHT synthesis; ambiguous female external genitalia at birth with dramatic virilization at puberty due to surging testosterone", "Endocrine Society Guidelines on Disorders of Sexual Development", "https://www.endocrine.org/"),
    ("Mullerian Agenesis (Mayer-Rokitansky-Kuster-Hauser Syndrome) 46,XX Absent Uterus Normal Ovaries and Secondary Sex Characteristics", "Genetics", "Pregnancy", "congenital failure of paramesonephric duct fusion causing absent uterus and upper vagina in 46,XX female with completely normal functional ovaries, normal estrogen, and pubertal development", "ACOG Committee Opinion: Mullerian Agenesis", "https://www.acog.org/"),
    ("Turner Syndrome 45,XO Complete or Mosaic Paternal X Monosomy Streak Ovaries and Coarctation of Aorta", "Genetics", "Pregnancy", "meiotic non-disjunction causing 45,X karyotype presenting with short stature, webbed neck, bicuspid aortic valve, aortic coarctation, streak gonads, and hypergonadotropic hypogonadism", "Turner Syndrome Clinical Practice Guidelines", "https://www.turnersyndrome.org/"),
    ("Klinefelter Syndrome 47,XXY Meiotic Nondisjunction Dysgenesis of Seminiferous Tubules Elevated FSH and LH", "Genetics", "Endocrine", "supernumerary X chromosome causing testicular atrophy, Leydig cell failure, low testosterone, elevated gonadotropins, eunuchoid tall stature, gynecomastia, and azoospermia", "Endocrine Society Guidelines on Male Hypogonadism", "https://www.endocrine.org/"),
    ("Kallmann Syndrome Defective KAL1 Anosmin-1 Neural Crest Migration Anosmia and Hypogonadotropic Hypogonadism", "Genetics", "Endocrine", "failure of GnRH-secreting olfactory neurons to migrate from olfactory placode into hypothalamus, causing low GnRH, low LH/FSH, low sex steroids, absent puberty, and anosmia", "Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guidelines", "https://www.endocrine.org/"),
    ("Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) Elevated LH-to-FSH Ratio Insulin Resistance and Ovarian Hyperthecosis", "Physiology", "Endocrine", "high-frequency GnRH pulses driving excess LH stimulation of ovarian theca cells producing androstenedione, converted by adipose aromatase to estrone, suppressing FSH and arresting follicles", "ACOG Practice Bulletin: Polycystic Ovary Syndrome", "https://www.acog.org/"),
    ("Granulosa Cell Tumor of Ovary Inhibin Secretion Call-Exner Bodies Estrogen Overproduction Endometrial Hyperplasia", "Pathology", "Pregnancy", "malignant sex cord-stromal ovarian neoplasm in postmenopausal females hypersecreting estrogen and inhibin, showing microfollicular Call-Exner bodies surrounding eosinophilic fluid", "SGO Clinical Practice Guidelines on Ovarian Neoplasms", "https://www.sgo.org/"),
    ("Leydig Cell Tumor Reinke Crystals Testosterone Secretion Precocious Puberty or Gynecomastia", "Pathology", "Endocrine", "sex cord-stromal testicular neoplasm composed of polygonal cells containing characteristic rod-shaped cytoplasmic Reinke crystalloids, hypersecreting androgens or estrogens", "AUA Practice Guidelines on Testicular Cancer", "https://www.auanet.org/"),
    ("Seminoma Testicular Germ Cell Neoplasm Large Cells with Watery Glycoplasmic Clear Cytoplasm c-Kit / CD117 Positive", "Pathology", "Renal", "most common malignant testicular tumor in young men; radiosensitive germ cell tumor showing sheets of uniform polygonal clear cells separated by fibrous septa with lymphocytes", "NCCN Practice Guidelines on Testicular Cancer", "https://www.nccn.org/"),
    ("Yolk Sac Tumor (Endodermal Sinus Tumor) Schiller-Duval Bodies Elevated Alpha-Fetoprotein (AFP)", "Pathology", "Renal", "most common testicular tumor in boys < 3 years; friable yellow-white mass exhibiting Schiller-Duval bodies resembling primitive glomeruli, with markedly elevated serum AFP", "NCCN Guidelines on Testicular Cancer", "https://www.nccn.org/"),
    ("Embryonal Carcinoma Aggressive Testicular Germ Cell Tumor Hemorrhage Necrosis Elevated hCG and AFP", "Pathology", "Renal", "highly malignant, painful, hemorrhagic mass with sheets of undifferentiated anaplastic epithelial cells forming primitive tubular glands, invading tunica albuginea early", "NCCN Guidelines on Testicular Cancer", "https://www.nccn.org/"),
    ("Choriocarcinoma Syncytiotrophoblasts and Cytotrophoblasts Widespread Hematogenous Cannonball Lung Metastases Elevated hCG", "Pathology", "Pregnancy", "highly aggressive gestational or non-gestational germ cell tumor lacking chorionic villi, hypersecreting beta-hCG and spreading hematogenously to lungs and brain early", "NCCN Guidelines on Gestational Trophoblastic Neoplasia", "https://www.nccn.org/"),
    ("Complete Hydatidiform Mole 46,XX All Paternal Chromosomes Snowstorm Pattern Markedly Elevated hCG", "Genetics", "Pregnancy", "fertilization of enucleated ovum by single sperm that duplicates (androgenesis); diffuse trophoblastic hyperplasia, generalized hydropic villi, absence of fetal parts, and high choriocarcinoma risk", "ACOG Practice Bulletin on Gestational Trophoblastic Disease", "https://www.acog.org/"),
    ("Partial Hydatidiform Mole 69,XXY Triploid Fertilization of Normal Ovum by Two Sperm", "Genetics", "Pregnancy", "diandric triploidy containing maternal and paternal chromosomes; focal hydropic swelling of chorionic villi with present fetal embryonic tissue, scalloped borders, and low malignancy risk", "ACOG Guidelines on Trophoblastic Disease", "https://www.acog.org/"),
