    # 121-150: Respiratory Mechanics, Gas Exchange & Cardiopulmonary Pathophysiology
    ("Alveolar Gas Equation PAO2 = (FiO2 x [P_atm - P_H2O]) - (PaCO2 / R) Hypoventilation Normal A-a Gradient", "Physiology", "Respiratory", "calculation of ideal alveolar oxygen tension where normal A-a gradient (typically < 10-15 mm Hg in young adult) confirms pure alveolar hypoventilation or high altitude as cause of hypoxemia", "ATS Core Curriculum in Pulmonary Physiology", "https://www.thoracic.org/"),
    ("A-a Oxygen Gradient Elevation V/Q Mismatch vs Shunt Supplemental Oxygen Response", "Physiology", "Respiratory", "widened A-a gradient signifies pulmonary parenchymal or vascular pathology; V/Q mismatch corrects with 100% FiO2, whereas right-to-left anatomical or physiological shunt fails to correct", "ATS Core Physiology Curriculum", "https://www.thoracic.org/"),
    ("Oxyhemoglobin Dissociation Curve Rightward Shift (Bohr Effect) Temperature Acidosis 2,3-BPG", "Physiology", "Hematology", "increased P50 and decreased hemoglobin oxygen affinity facilitating unloading of O2 to active peripheral tissues promoted by elevated H+ (acidosis), high PaCO2, elevated temperature, and 2,3-BPG", "ASH Physiology Curriculum", "https://www.hematology.org/"),
    ("Oxyhemoglobin Dissociation Curve Leftward Shift Alkalosis Hypothermia Fetal Hemoglobin (HbF) Carboxyhemoglobin", "Physiology", "Hematology", "decreased P50 and increased hemoglobin oxygen affinity holding O2 tightly promoted by low PaCO2, alkalosis, hypothermia, low 2,3-BPG, HbF (gamma chains), and carbon monoxide poisoning", "ASH Physiology Curriculum", "https://www.hematology.org/"),
    ("Carbon Monoxide Poisoning Carboxyhemoglobin Formation Left Shift and Normal PaO2 with Reduced SaO2", "Pathology", "Hematology", "CO binds hemoglobin with 240-fold greater affinity than oxygen forming carboxyhemoglobin, locking remaining heme tetramers in relaxed high-affinity state and starving tissues", "ACMT Practice Guidelines on Carbon Monoxide Toxicity", "https://www.acmt.net/"),
    ("Methemoglobinemia Oxidation of Ferrous (Fe2+) to Ferric (Fe3+) Iron Cyanosis 'Chocolate Brown Blood' Methylene Blue", "Pharmacology", "Hematology", "oxidative stress from nitrates, dapsone, or benzocaine oxidizing heme iron to Fe3+, which cannot bind oxygen; pulse oximetry locks at ~85%; treated with reducing agent methylene blue", "ACMT Guidelines on Methemoglobinemia", "https://www.acmt.net/"),
    ("Physiological Dead Space Bohr Equation (V_D / V_T = [PaCO2 - P_ECO2] / PaCO2) Pulmonary Embolism", "Physiology", "Respiratory", "alveoli that are ventilated but under-perfused (V/Q ratio approaching infinity); acute vascular occlusion by pulmonary embolism acutely enlarges physiological dead space", "ATS Core Physiology Reviews", "https://www.thoracic.org/"),
    ("Work of Breathing Elastic vs Flow-Resistive Work Minimization in Obstructive vs Restrictive Disease", "Physiology", "Respiratory", "restrictive lung disease patients breathe with rapid shallow respirations to minimize high elastic work; obstructive patients breathe with slow deep breaths to minimize flow resistance", "ATS Pulmonary Mechanics Curriculum", "https://www.thoracic.org/"),
    ("Pulmonary Surfactant Dipalmitoylphosphatidylcholine (DPPC) Law of Laplace Reduction of Surface Tension", "Physiology", "Respiratory", "type II pneumocyte secretion of DPPC reducing surface tension in small alveoli (P = 2T/r), preventing end-expiratory alveolar atelectasis and increasing lung compliance", "AAP Guidelines on Neonatal Respiratory Distress", "https://www.aap.org/"),
    ("Lung Compliance Hysteresis Intermolecular Attractive Forces at Air-Liquid Interface", "Physiology", "Respiratory", "greater pressure required to inflate a deflated fluid-lined lung than to deflate it due to high initial surface tension forces that must be overcome during alveolar recruitment", "ATS Pulmonary Physiology Curriculum", "https://www.thoracic.org/"),
    ("Obstructive Lung Disease Spirometry Decreased FEV1/FVC Ratio < 0.70 Air Trapping and Hyperinflation", "Physiology", "Respiratory", "expiratory airflow limitation causing marked decline in FEV1 with preserved or elevated total lung capacity (TLC) and residual volume (RV), shifting flow-volume loop to the left", "GOLD Global Strategy for COPD", "https://goldcopd.org/"),
    ("Restrictive Lung Disease Spirometry Normal or Increased FEV1/FVC Ratio Reduced Total Lung Capacity < 80%", "Physiology", "Respiratory", "parenchymal fibrosis or chest wall deformities reducing lung expansion, producing proportional reductions in both FEV1 and FVC (FEV1/FVC >= 0.70) with reduced DLCO in intrinsic disease", "ATS/ERS Guidelines on Pulmonary Function Testing", "https://www.thoracic.org/"),
    ("Diffusing Capacity of the Lung for Carbon Monoxide (DLCO) Alveolar-Capillary Membrane Surface Area", "Physiology", "Respiratory", "measures gas transfer efficiency; reduced in emphysema (capillary destruction), idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis, and pulmonary hypertension; normal in chronic bronchitis and asthma", "ATS/ERS Standards for DLCO", "https://www.thoracic.org/"),
    ("High Altitude Adaptation Hyperventilation Respiratory Alkalosis Compensatory Renal Bicarbonate Excretion", "Physiology", "Respiratory", "hypobaric hypoxia sensed by peripheral carotid body chemoreceptors driving hyperventilation; acute respiratory alkalosis is compensated over 48-72h by renal wasting of bicarbonate", "Wilderness Medical Society Guidelines on High Altitude Illness", "https://wms.org/"),
    ("Exercise Physiology Cardiopulmonary Response Constant PaO2 and PaCO2 Mixed Venous Blood Oxygen Depletion", "Physiology", "Cardiovascular", "strenuous exercise increases alveolar ventilation and cardiac output proportionally to metabolic rate, maintaining arterial PaO2 and PaCO2 normal while venous oxygen saturation drops dramatically", "ACSM Guidelines for Exercise Testing", "https://www.acsm.org/"),
    ("Hypoxic Pulmonary Vasoconstriction Euler-Liljestrand Mechanism Shunting Blood to Well-Ventilated Alveoli", "Physiology", "Respiratory", "alveolar hypoxia directly inhibits voltage-gated potassium channels in pulmonary arterial smooth muscle, depolarizing membrane and constricting arterioles to optimize V/Q matching", "ATS Core Pulmonary Circulation Curriculum", "https://www.thoracic.org/"),
    ("Centriacinar Emphysema Smoking Predilection for Upper Lung Lobes Protease-Antiprotease Imbalance", "Pathology", "Respiratory", "cigarette smoke recruits neutrophils and macrophages releasing elastase, destroying central respiratory bronchioles while sparing distal alveoli, predominantly in apical lung zones", "GOLD Guidelines for COPD", "https://goldcopd.org/"),
    ("Panacinar Emphysema Alpha-1 Antitrypsin Deficiency Predilection for Lower Lung Lobes", "Genetics", "Respiratory", "systemic uninhibited neutrophil elastase activity causing uniform destruction of entire acinus from respiratory bronchiole to terminal alveoli, predominantly involving lung bases", "ATS Guidelines on AATD", "https://www.thoracic.org/"),
    ("Neonatal Respiratory Distress Syndrome Low Lecithin-to-Sphingomyelin Ratio (< 2.0) Hyaline Membranes", "Pathology", "Respiratory", "prematurity before 34 weeks gestation with deficient surfactant production; collapse of alveoli creates ischemic injury, fibrin exudation, and eosinophilic hyaline membranes", "AAP Neonatal Respiratory Distress Guidelines", "https://www.aap.org/"),
